Issue #1968: PIT Stage 12 W8.3 — Project hierarchy pre-build alignment and implementation readiness

## Purpose

Prepare the next governed PIT Stage 12 product wave after completed Slice 4.

The target product boundary is the hierarchy beneath an existing Supabase-backed project:

`Project → Milestones → Deliverables → Tasks / Action Items`

This issue is a **pre-build alignment and readiness wave**. It does not appoint a builder and does not authorise runtime implementation until the required authority artifacts, QA-to-RED contract and IAA pre-brief are complete and accepted.

## Authority

- CS2 Authority: Johan Ras
- Parent Stage 12 authority: #1767
- Approved implementation-plan wave: W8.3
- Completed predecessor: Issue #1943 / PR #1952
- Post-merge reconciliation: Issue #1964 / PR #1965
- Foreman orchestration: required

## Product boundary to freeze

### Hierarchy

- a project contains milestones;
- a milestone contains deliverables;
- a deliverable contains tasks/action items;
- each child remains bound to the parent project and organisation;
- parent-child ordering, status and date semantics must be deterministic;
- the hierarchy must provide structurally valid inputs for later timeline, assignment and progress-roll-up waves.

### Routes and workspaces

- `/projects/:id`
- `/projects/:id/milestones`
- `/projects/:id/deliverables`
- `/projects/:id/tasks`
- `/projects/:id/settings`

### Roles and denied paths

Freeze creator, project leader, owner and viewer permissions for hierarchy create/read/update/archive actions. Cross-organisation and unauthenticated access must remain denied.

## Required pre-build work

1. Reconcile W8.3 against the approved App Description, UX/Wiring, FRS, TRS, Architecture, QA-to-RED catalog, PBFAG and Stage 8 implementation plan.
2. Define the exact Supabase hierarchy schema and repository contracts.
3. Define lifecycle semantics, including active/complete/archived handling; do not introduce unsafe hard deletion as a normal user action.
4. Define parent-child, date-order, status-transition and orphan-prevention invariants.
5. Map W8.3 requirements to `PROJECT-001..016`, `ROUTE-010`, `ROUTE-012..014` and `ROUTE-017` without weakening the established RED baseline.
6. Produce the W8.3 QA-to-RED contract before implementation.
7. Produce Foreman QP, ECAP administrative evidence and an independent IAA pre-brief.
8. Produce a builder checklist and explicit GO/NO-GO recommendation for appointment.

## Explicit exclusions

This issue must not implement or claim:

- assignment, invitation, notification or My Work loops — W8.4;
- evidence upload/review/approval or audit export — W8.5;
- timeline/date-grid or dependency engine — W8.6;
- progress roll-up, RAG or watchdog — W8.7;
- reporting/export — W8.8;
- AIMC functionality — W8.9;
- full route/LFV closure — W8.10;
- full PIT, Stage 12, production-readiness or `FUNCTIONAL_PASS` completion;
- closure of separate Issue #1944.

## Readiness exit criteria

- W8.3 scope and route boundary frozen;
- data and API contracts approved;
- RLS/role matrix and negative paths approved;
- lifecycle and archive semantics approved;
- QA-to-RED contract committed and demonstrably RED for the missing hierarchy;
- IAA pre-brief completed;
- Foreman returns an explicit Stage 11 appointment GO/NO-GO;
- no implementation builder appointed before all readiness criteria are satisfied.

## Current disposition

`PRE-BUILD ALIGNMENT REQUIRED — BUILDER APPOINTMENT NO-GO`

