  - type: bypassed_abstraction
    severity: high
    description: Code bypasses documented abstraction layer
    example: "Direct database access instead of Repository pattern"
    remediation: "Use proper abstraction layer or update constitution if pattern has changed"

  - type: parallel_implementation
    severity: medium
    description: Similar logic implemented in multiple places
    example: "Invoice validation logic in 3 different services"
    remediation: "Extract common logic to shared service"

  - type: ownership_violation
    severity: medium
    description: File modified by wrong owner or team
    example: "TitanPay code modified by payment-team instead of security-team"
    remediation: "Review changes or update ownership rules"

  - type: circular_dependency
    severity: critical
    description: Circular dependency detected in service graph
    example: "ServiceA -> ServiceB -> ServiceC -> ServiceA"
    remediation: "Break circular dependency by introducing third service or interface"

  - type: untested_critical_code
    severity: high
    description: Critical business logic has no test coverage
    example: "PaymentReconciliation logic not tested"
    remediation: "Add test coverage for critical paths"

  - type: dead_code
    severity: low
    description: Reachable code is never actually called at runtime
    example: "PaymentGateway::legacyRetryLogic() never invoked"
    remediation: "Remove if truly obsolete or document why it's retained"

  - type: undocumented_public_api
    severity: low
    description: Public service method lacks documentation
    example: "PaymentService::reconcile() has no docblock or tests"
    remediation: "Add docblock and examples documenting usage"

  - type: security_policy_violation
    severity: critical
    description: Code violates documented security policy
    example: "shell_exec() used despite being forbidden"
    remediation: "Remove forbidden code or update security policy"

