You said *"when there are multiple layers of nesting it might be required to have iterative generation"*. It is, and here is the bound, because this is the case I expected to kill the design.

A model that nests **itself** (`Comment` holding `IReadOnlyList<Comment>`) looks like it needs an infinite parameter list. It doesn't — **F-bounded polymorphism closes the loop in one parameter**:

```csharp
public interface ICommentBase<TComment> where TComment : ICommentBase<TComment>
{
    string Text { get; set; }
    IReadOnlyList<TComment> Replies { get; set; }
}
public interface IComment : ICommentBase<Comment> { }
public class Comment : CommentBase<Comment>, IComment { }
```

