## Problem

V0.1 discovers child sheets but does not recursively merge them into one project-level electrical graph. Real hardware projects commonly use hierarchical sheets, so an agent can currently miss cross-sheet connectivity.

## Goal

Extend the KiCad adapter so a project can resolve components, labels, and nets across hierarchical child sheets while preserving conservative connectivity semantics.

## Acceptance criteria

- recursively load referenced child `.kicad_sch` files within the configured workspace root;
- preserve sheet path / origin information in the canonical model;
- resolve hierarchical labels without inventing cross-sheet connections;
- detect recursive/cyclic sheet references safely;
- add small synthetic fixtures covering at least one parent + child sheet and one nested hierarchy;
- add regression tests and parser warnings for unresolved or missing child sheets;
- document the behavior and known KiCad-version limitations.

## Design constraint

Keep hierarchy handling inside the KiCad adapter/canonical model. MCP tools should remain format-neutral.

Contributions and compatibility fixtures are welcome, but fixtures must be synthetic or explicitly redistributable.

