A maintainer on the project wgt-system/wiiii-got-this (unknown) filed this issue about hand-rolled graph machinery causing pain:

Issue #53: Refine Atlas dossier and hosted-product rail for persistent capability control

## Goal

Turn the current Atlas inspector/dossier and hosted-product rail into durable product chrome that supports the living-world interaction model instead of behaving like a transient graph popover.

## Atlas dossier / inspector

Current physical World smoke shows the content direction is useful, but the panel behavior and nested-card styling are not yet acceptable.

Required behavior:
- selecting a world object opens one persistent floating dossier;
- the dossier must **not jump/swap left-right when the Atlas camera pans or zooms**;
- panel position is user-controlled and remains stable until explicitly moved/closed;
- make the panel draggable by an appropriate header area;
- close `X` belongs in the top-right corner;
- remove taxonomy/debug chips such as `PRODUCT` / `COMPOSED` from normal presentation;
- show connection state with a compact semantic status icon + text instead of extra chips;
- keep the existing tab model (`Node`, `Caps`, `Links`, `Data`, `Device`, `Diag`) unless physical UX proves a better structure;
- avoid card-inside-card presentation for ordinary facts: prefer flat sections, rows, typography and dividers;
- primary action (`Open Vocation`, `Open Illumination`, etc.) remains a real button but is pinned at the **bottom of the dossier and visible across all tabs**;
- enabling/disabling/configuration remains explicit and must not be triggered by decorative world interactions.

## Hosted Product rail

When a provider Product Surface is open, the WGT-owned left rail should become a fast context/control surface rather than only a Return-to-Atlas strip.

Direction:
- WGT/Atlas entry remains at the top;
- WGT-global capabilities/settings/tools appear in a WGT-owned section beneath it;
- provider identity appears as the next clear section boundary;
- provider-local capabilities/controls appear beneath the provider identity as flat icon actions;
- each section may scroll independently or the rail may use one compact scroll model when counts grow;
- capability controls must remain usable when a product has many local capabilities;
- icons/tooltips/accessibility names must explain actions without requiring the user to know service/repository architecture;
- WGT-global and provider-local actions must remain visually distinguishable;
- provider-specific business UI stays provider-owned; the rail is WGT host/control chrome only.

## Acceptance

- dossier position does not change merely because the camera moves;
- user can drag and close the dossier predictably;
- close button is top-right;
- no normal-product `PRODUCT`/`COMPOSED` badge clutter;
- ordinary dossier content is flat rather than nested cards;
- primary Open/Enable action stays visible at dossier bottom across tabs;
- hosted-product rail demonstrates separate WGT-global and provider-local sections with scroll-safe capability actions;
- keyboard/focus/touch paths remain available;
- Reduced Motion does not remove state meaning;
- physical Windows smoke confirms the panel/rail behavior before closure.

Tracked under #46; World visual renderer remains #51 and capability topology #52.

